WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.001 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-You brought them in.

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.335
I can't believe these are
the headphones that you,

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:06.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
a television personality,
you are actually --

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:09.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
actively running with
these headphones?

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.845 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:13.046 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:16.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
Needless to say you
had to get the attachment.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.517 line:92%
It looks like -- were these,

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:21.087
did these used to be a chew toy
for your old iguana?

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.322 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.356 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They're crazy.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What's wrong with
the headphones?

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:25.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They look like --
well, first of all,

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:27.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
if I saw somebody
jogging by with this,

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:31.331 size:84% position:42%
I would assume they had
started in the past.

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:33.500 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:38.671 line:92%
They had run from the past.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.373 line:92%
-Everyone who sees those says,

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:43.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
"How did you get those vintage
headphones?"

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:44.711 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:47.547
And I say that I got them
at Duane Reade last week,

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they're still
selling them.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, really? Is that true?
-Yes.

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:51.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, I will say,
I don't want totally

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:54.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
run down these headphones,
because I do believe --

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:56.589
I'm serious.
I'm going to say something true.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.091
I don't use brand-new headphones
either.

00:00:58.091 --> 00:01:01.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
I -- I find an old --
there's like a Sony headphone

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.196
that goes over the ear,
because normal headphones

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:05.198
fall out of my ear immediately,
and these stay on.

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:09.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, if you've got a little
raisinette in your ear,

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:12.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't see why
that's better than this.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:16.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nothing -- no one
can pull these off.

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:17.911 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.947 line:92%
This is an air-tight operation.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.482 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Now on your commute --

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:25.318 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:28.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you had to --
I'm assuming this

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:32.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the first time anyone's
wrapped these up, yeah.

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My children are here.
Thank you so much.

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.029
-Have you had to do any errands
on your run?

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:38.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you had to do any sweaty
errands on your commute?

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:41.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah, well --
now, I like to combine

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
a run and an errand, too.
-Yeah.

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:46.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But the problem with that
is you've got your cash

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:49.476 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in your sports bra.

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:51.010 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Maybe you guys don't.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:51.544 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:54.914
If you have another option,
please tell me afterwards,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:55.982 size:88% position:44% line:92%
but I keep my cash here.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:59.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then so when you go to
pay for something

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.587 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and you're, like --

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:01.988 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Panting ]

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:02.789 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:06.326
And hand them a dollar bill
that has like, wilted already --

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:08.628 size:84% position:42%
people don't want that.
-They don't want that.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:11.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They'd rather keep
their merchandise than --

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:14.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Even from a celeb,
they don't want it.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:17.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They don't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:20.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to talk briefly
before --

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:23.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
You played Giuliani
a couple of weeks ago.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:26.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I did, didn't I?

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:29.282 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-How was that?

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:31.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you know,
this was a --

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:33.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was not my idea,
I want to say.

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:36.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was the idea
of one of our best

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
and most wonderful writers,
Kent Sublette, I guess.

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:43.363
And he said the night before,
do you want to do Giuliani?

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:45.632 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And I said..."Yeah?"

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:46.399 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:50.236
Okay. Turns out,
it wasn't as hard as I thought,

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we have something
in common

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:54.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is that we
both go like this.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.877 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:00.647 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:03.216 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And I've been -- Yeah.

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:05.585 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-So it was secretly...

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:08.721 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:11.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, he maybe was stealing
the move from you.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:15.061
-I think he was, because I've
been doing it a long time.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:18.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm so happy for you that
you are going to have a break,

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:19.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're going to do a show
on Saturday.

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:23.403
And then you're going to have
the summer to do other things.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:24.270 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Well-deserved.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.706
I can't wait, of course,
for you to come back next year.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks.
-Kate McKinnon, everybody.

